Dear Mr. Illsley;
Your letter and its enclosures to Harper and Brothers made me very happy, and encouraged me greatly in future endeavors for the publication of my book, "The Invisible Gods." 
It is quite true that aside from its temp[[?]] [[?]] of history, its central idea should be valid for all time--if only I could make a re-publisher think so! I have no influential friends of Harlem - and I suppose they may be

